   "he": "עָמִיר כִּמְלֹא פִי טָלֶה. וְהָתַנְיָא כִּגְרוֹגֶרֶת! אִידֵּי וְאִידֵּי חַד שִׁיעוּרָא הוּא.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: The measure that determines liability for «an ear of grain» is «equivalent to a lamb’s mouthful.» The Gemara asks: «Wasn’t it taught» in a baraita: Its measure for liability is «equivalent to a dried fig-bulk?» The Gemara explains: «This,» a lamb’s mouthful, «and that,» a dried fig-bulk, «are one,» the same, «measure.»"
  }
